# Who must approve a change, enforced by GitHub rather than by the fleet.
#
# `docs/IDENTITY.md` states the principle the whole arrangement rests on: the
# app may change the work, and may never change the rules that govern the
# work. Until now that was enforced only by `agent-branches.yml`, which
# refuses to auto-merge anything under `.github/` or `.claude/` -- a rule the
# automation applies to itself, in a file the automation can write to.
#
# The circle closes because editing that workflow is itself a `.github/`
# change, so it needs a human too. But it closes by argument, not by
# mechanism, and an argument is not a gate. This is the gate: GitHub will not
# merge a change to these paths without the owner's approval, and the fleet
# cannot reach the setting that says so.
#
# Deliberately short. Everything not listed here is the fleet's, which is the
# point -- the author controls the book by controlling the fleet, not by
# reviewing its output.

# The automation, and the briefs that tell it what it may do.
/.github/   @bugabinga
/.claude/   @bugabinga
